{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:2a6782f363653801e8e45059d6d40c5fcbf0c19dd24f7f8fd6618e58bb587ed3","title":"The setting isolates the two tensor polarizations of metric perturbations on a spatially flat expanding universe. Ashtekar variables make their Hamiltonian evolution accessible to corrections motivated by a loop quantization.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0003"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2aa89e48e9babfa81f4bbda4871060131383639b247890aa94994ea6c641c5e8","title":"How should axionic hypermultiplet fields be continued to Euclidean signature, including charge-dependent boundary terms, to construct real instanton and wormhole saddles with positive action? Which solutions preserve supersymmetry or survive N=1 orientifold projections?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a5415c009e4ebfc381ff601f91eea9ff6f766f8fbbe3a98c50f5e5d68fa16a5","title":"Can two axions support high-scale, chaotic-like inflation with a superplanckian trajectory inside a region of subplanckian diameter, while suppressing an η problem and easing control constraints in a string realization?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a1ca10ffa95cc2cd2da4457d705b70319c53e449b5f8d782ecf7953e4be7e5e","title":"Can electrically excited acoustic resonances constrain non-neutrality of matter, and does reanalysis support the sensitivity previously claimed for the 1973 acoustic experiment?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0010"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a2d2871325df605de4f082155d18353ee76008c8d0535fc31d2fd4fae0b5ca5","title":"Under which quantum error-correction conditions are a quantum-corrected RT formula, complementary entanglement-wedge reconstruction, and equality of bulk and boundary relative entropies equivalent? How can the area operator remain nontrivial?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0022"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a318d6c0fc4e76b1e37c89ec6a8a9ef51a3024035014ffbfe3c2de85e42d31b","title":"How can structure-sheaf cohomology h^i(O_D) of square-free divisors in toric Calabi–Yau threefold hypersurfaces be computed efficiently, including at large h^{1,1}, to supply data relevant to Euclidean-brane zero modes and nonperturbative superpotentials?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a4208f7deca5a77e25fef94b52c3684bbbb84d8c98bbe839af77ec1325a8aab","title":"How closely do elliptic Calabi–Yau threefolds constructed through Weierstrass/Tate tunings reproduce toric hypersurface constructions at large Hodge numbers, and how do Tate tunings correspond to polytope tops?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0029"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a97a8c8aba4dddccfae9aa3ab3353773c2b34123cfa733c16177fe9d75c16f7","title":"Can curvature generate massive modes below the internal momentum towers? Fixing the twist and enlarging the base relative to the fiber gives |f|≪1/r¹,1/r²≪1/r³.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0029"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a162f6afbb5f0d773f713b5991c923c6f410a5b07637dcfc53bfadcf7d48b86","title":"The QCD axion dynamically relaxes the strong CP angle. The paper asks whether the periodic potential needed for this mechanism is compatible with a derivative bound on the full potential when quintessence is its only light spectator.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0032"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a5988b0e2e636d6c71428765de1052bcf18e2ba5acaa3c949ea1673aa6878ae","title":"What prevents a compelling quantum description of cosmology in string theory? The appendix emphasizes time dependence, nonsupersymmetric backgrounds, singularities and cosmological observables, while arguing that current technical limitations are insufficient grounds to dismiss the program.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a6539ca3a94c2a6d09d77704e13eb441d56e988608c60b3caa93cb7d9652c10","title":"Do cosmological distance and perturbation measurements permit canonical dark energy with an order-one potential slope or negative curvature, and do inferred field excursions challenge a Planck-scale distance limit?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2af9bbb5b0f269e589d9995316c6656b96261dbcfd5df62b0d011ac75ba4672d","title":"How sensitive is nonsymmetric hyperinflation to initial position and transverse motion? The reported tests include five trajectories and transverse-to-gradient initial velocity ratios down to 10^−10.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0038"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2af235ec954a736d318bc8bbdea00d3cd91e17931b5deb5af04564b8c2bc4fe0","title":"Do modular-inflation quotient geometries satisfy the volume, distance, and topology criteria the authors associate with a possible quantum-gravity completion?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2acf2e165d284872cc674da3477d42164092f746d47c1ccc727f20fba6ee4e7d","title":"Do curved kinetic terms destabilize ultra-light axionic isocurvature modes in Fibre Inflation, and can nonperturbative axion masses remove the instability while preserving the usual leading inflationary dynamics?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a1a9054d9c9eaea53258bd91a043b18d094f957c49c00e2f9f89f2f4bf44547","title":"Could environmental or nonlinear screening hide a gravity-strength scalar interaction from the experiments used in the exclusion? The paper names Vainshtein and Chameleon mechanisms but leaves both their effectiveness here and their quantum-gravity compatibility unresolved.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a381bd49c66b3c9d2ca626bbb6a74ef1e930a95de8e042839b64246011c7c13","title":"Could the emergence of a light tower during quintessence evolution already affect dark matter? The paper asks whether a recent decrease of dark-matter mass can ease discrepancies between early-universe inference and local H0 or weak-lensing observations.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0043"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2af8f302067053b8e9134cd25232d8dc814ad0b8bcb1ba6f6d2bf4b3aef3696e","title":"What restrictions do dense towers of superextremal instantons impose on large-field axion inflation once the full charge-lattice sum is included, and which effective theories can evade those restrictions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0047"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a4e4bb8fabc0ad9a9dd3862e39146d449b7fb138ee6df1dcdc0e37670e8d4c1","title":"Does prohibiting trans-Planckian fluctuations from becoming classical constrain complete effective theories, or selected cosmological histories? An unobserved allowed history could exclude a theory and thereby restrict its observable predictions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a9332901d265cbbfa85fa51e0fca50ad3ba24b99c0580ef52879e90afb09026","title":"What consistency mechanism enforces the production inequality, and how does it connect to black-hole physics? Open extensions include AdS and de Sitter backgrounds, higher dimensions, non-Abelian mediators, massive moduli, and multifield strong bounds.","connectionCount":0,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2abb832ff7edfe528660455b2cc47b5276e2db395694705f0f5316abc4ec5d60","title":"Which late-time observations constrain the local expansion without extending distance approximations too far? The selected inputs combine direct expansion-rate information, two sufficiently low-redshift isotropic BAO points and supernova-derived normalized Hubble rates.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a257f8d2e1e110d5144a69538f05774415390166c6663ed8b76faf2cd246753","title":"Can boundary algebraic data reconstruct the asymptotic geometry of Calabi–Yau moduli spaces and exclude infinite sequences of flux vacua approaching their boundaries?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0058"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a5d1e8df6529c1227a3e2afb812e04870092d78fc2ea424826bacf1d1264777","title":"Can the anomaly-compatible T=0 su(2) spectrum with two half-hypermultiplets in the 4 representation be realized geometrically? The proposed realization requires a degree-five curve on P² with two distinct triple points.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0060"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a18ea276893d6ae1d5e08758ce56976eea46ba47725212d38474ddc3a3191a5","title":"How can source-free scalar behavior and regular horizon electrostatics be imposed efficiently in a nonlinear holographic boundary problem?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0060"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a1c78fe256ecc1b5de2bb536ebd7dc9654b580bb830d88955e45302b1ed90ea","title":"Can relativistic cosmologies have finite past-to-present saddle actions despite divergent curvature or matter density?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0062"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2add721a2c187da46197d34fc1c6cc58c185b6259dbc13fc878c099bd450eb7f","title":"What monodromies occur when a discrete gauge transformation changes a continuous charge or permutes entire gauge sectors?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0064"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a2124576413b39c5abc0029b9d9bc63456515a23c31c3db8328427fedd37df9","title":"The local setting isolates the instability of an axion placed close to the maximum of a periodic potential. Negative potential curvature competes with Hubble damping and determines how rapidly the field leaves its initial position.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0064"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a33225bea83cbbad0f22f262d3c164f953d2712f1fc5a95ea57418aff6c4a41","title":"How can one realize many copies of a QFT with different constant couplings inside one string construction?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0069"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a2f5d7da87c8f495f48818d4d1cb110e3e4801d32705fb37de1333ad830968d","title":"Which freely acting type IIB orbifolds yield five-dimensional Minkowski vacua with spontaneous supersymmetry breaking, and what mass quantization, modular invariance, integrality and massless-spectrum constraints govern their Scherk–Schwarz descriptions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0080"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a2c060a46d220877bd5228dfda3f59b0a5a9e3b16caa1f41e43aa1a093298ad","title":"How do noncommutative smearing, Gauss–Bonnet coupling, charge and a string cloud affect horizons, photon spheres and timelike circular orbits, and can configurations retaining horizons at q/m>1 serve as candidates for studying WGC protection of WCCC?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0091"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2ab023fb30a63119a84492b5e7c49045cebe6bd46e9cb48cc6286d55fd9e2e9b","title":"How does Starobinsky inflation fare as a gravitational effective theory when confronted with CMB observations, primordial-black-hole production, quantum-gravity conjectures, string corrections and reheating? This memorial contribution primarily reviews existing results.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0092"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a5ba695c08eac2c09afe8bfa63a36a8acba0a73a5fbbeb0f6db08757003e84b","title":"Does the minimal charged-operator dimension satisfy Δ((n1+n2)q0) ≥ Δ(n1q0)+Δ(n2q0) for positive integers n1,n2, particularly at large charge? The paper examines the required charge spacing q0 and whether bottom-up EFT consistency can establish this conjecture.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0093"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a2ba189805c0d350b6df81dbc7866065b8acd45a6f7ebb55fd5940dc0db3123","title":"Can differential equations for moduli-dependent species scales explain asymptotic Swampland constraints, and can using that scale as a loop cutoff generate potentials that stabilize no-scale moduli?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0100"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a201687048523dd68a0aaedc4db33cadcae8f3b868b603289d5ae60f6d2a75a","title":"Which group-theoretic data determine Hagedorn growth at the overall free point of large-N four-dimensional N=2 Lagrangian SCFTs, and how do these data constrain CFT Distance Conjecture rates in partial-decoupling limits?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0101"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a292d9c1f609e6b7b62503b0606bbb682b3d64055262aad8acfa0e6be8c76b6","title":"Does third-order backreaction protect near-extremal GMGHS black holes against overcharging despite their finite-temperature extremal limit, and can an SDC tower provide dynamical discharge while relaxing the thermodynamic WGC bound?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0102"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a519da63343fe88bfa43e46ce4e737f716cb974e55f7513e7458400dff4569a","title":"How can scalar matter and gravitational perturbations be calculated accurately to first order in slow roll for arbitrarily many fields with nonminimal kinetic terms, including horizon crossing, trajectory rotation and entropy sourcing?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0105"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2ada564fa4201c489e6e0b30a665404fd6979827ae1db07cb4cba44fed4cf651","title":"How can second-quantized string theory and general particle field theories be formulated so that gauge covariance, physical degrees of freedom, and off-shell dynamics can be related systematically? The motivating goal includes eventual treatment of nonperturbative phenomena and manifest gauge, Lorentz, and spacetime supersymmetries.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0108"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2a64043bf83a01c4f7ef75dd8e65e4e946d818adc56648f7b9ee04e34a7ad051","title":"What do the O(e^−N) corrections that spoil large-N holomorphic factorization of two-dimensional Yang–Mills mean in the dual black-hole geometry, and can their baby-universe interpretation preserve quantum coherence?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0113"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:2aa6b6f43474b30eb4a85e7e552db99d9cde6040e0330cdf298fc52e8cdae719","title"